{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773076026,"nonce":"/wrprY+4FnaXbuxQHmmIGuGdsps=","title":"consoleStreamHandler reads payload.data (undefined) — stream events never dispatched, streaming forever","message":"In app.tsx, consoleStreamHandler checks payload.data before dispatching the CustomEvent. But SSE payloads are spread at the top level — there is no .data wrapper. The broadcast sends {console_session_id, event} which becomes the payload directly (type is added/promoted by parsePayload). So payload.data is always undefined, data is null, the handler returns early, and window.dispatchEvent is never called. Result: console:stream_event CustomEvents are never fired, TerminalPane SSE listener receives nothing, streaming state stays true forever after user sends a message. Fix: remove the payload.data check; just dispatch { detail: { ...payload } }.","files":null}]}